MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Some comments:

1. The problem occurs in the internal method getUnitGroupCellMap().
This is only called once per chip type, regardless if you restart R or
not.  The result is memoized (=cached to file) and reused in the
future.  Thus, if you can get it to work once, you won't have the
problem anymore.
2. It might help to try in a fresh R session.  See if this works.
3. It is *not* unlikely that the problem is because you are using the
default CDF.  So, Mark's suggests might be the best solution.
4. Try also extractDataFrame(fs, units=units) on a subset of units/the
units of interest.  That can circumvent the problematic huge units in
the default CDF.

/Henrik

