There is no 'names' argument of bxp() like there is for boxplot(), so
thats why this doesn't work.

However, the returned 'bpstats' above is a 'list' object.  The names
of this list, which come from the names of your original files, are
used as the labels in the plot.  Look at:

names(bpstats)  # these should match what you currently see

... and then you can override them with ...

names(bpstats) <- c("G1,"G2","G3") # just make sure that they match
the files correctly

HTH,
Mark

