>From what I can see there is a bug in the function
findUnitsTodo.ChipEffectFile.

The following code fragment is supposed to (I think) get one index per
unit, to be used to access the standard deviation for that index, and
test if that value is <= 0.

idxs <-
  lapplyInChunks(units,
                 function(unitsChunk,
                          ...
                          )
                 {
                   idxsChunk <-
                     getCellIndices(this,
                                    units = unitsChunk,
                                    force = TRUE,
                                    verbose = less(verbose)
                                    )
                   names(idxsChunk) <- NULL

                   idxsChunk <-
                     base::lapply(idxsChunk,
                                  FUN = function(unit)
                                  {
                                    groups <- .subset2(unit, "groups")
                                    fields <- .subset2(groups, 1)
                                    .subset2(fields, 1)
                                  }
                                  )
                   idxsChunk
                 },
                 chunkSize = 1e+05,
                 useNames = FALSE,
                 verbose = verbose
                 )

units <- units0
rm(units0)
idxs <- unlist(idxs, use.names = FALSE)

if (length(idxs) != nbrOfUnits)
{
  throw("Internal error: Expected ",
        nbrOfUnits,
        " cell indices, but got ",
        length(idxs), ".")
}

The assertion that length(idxs) == nbrOfUnits is a good one -- the
idea is to test one index per unit, so their lengths should match.
But this is where an error is being triggered when I exercise the
code.

I think the problem is with the innermost function,

FUN = function(unit)
  {
    groups <- .subset2(unit, "groups")
    fields <- .subset2(groups, 1)
    .subset2(fields, 1)
  }

The argument 'unit' which is passed to this function looks like

> unit
$groups
$groups$AG
$groups$AG$indices
[1] 7417 7418

so 'groups' and 'fields' look like

> groups
$AG
$AG$indices
[1] 7417 7418

> fields
$indices
[1] 7417 7418

and the returned value is

> .subset2(fields, 1)
[1] 7417 7418

I.e. this is a length-2 vector, not length one, which I think is
intended.

An alternative would be

FUN = function(unit)
  {
    groups <- .subset2(unit, "groups")
    fields <- .subset2(groups, 1)
    indices <- .subset2(fields, 1)
    .subset2(indices, 1)
  }

or perhaps

FUN = function(unit)
  unlist(unit)[1]

This does look like a bug to me. Please let me know if it is or if I
am misunderstanding something.  The code does work OK for 50K
platforms where a typical indices list ('unit') looks different:

